    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "An enemy brain as a finite state machine driven by a switch and a transition event.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ADVANCED 2/9: STATE MACHINE\nStates are integers held in the `state` variable: 0 Idle, 1 Patrol, 2 Chase, 3 Attack, 4 Dead.\nOne custom event, `change_state`, is the ONLY place state changes, so entering a state\n(reset the timer, log, start effects) always happens exactly once. on_tick runs the current\nstate's logic through a Switch on Int, and asks for transitions by dispatching change_state.",
        "position": [
          0,
          -270
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          170
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. START - enter the Idle state (0) by dispatching the transition event. The literal 0 is typed\nstraight into the `new_state` pin of the dispatch node.",
        "position": [
          -40,
          -80
        ],
        "size": [
          680,
          270
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "bp_enter"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. TRANSITION HANDLER - the `change_state` custom event (red hexagon in the Events panel).\nOrder matters: remember the previous state, store the new one, reset the per-state timer,\nthen Switch on Int picks the \"on enter\" log for the new state. Add per-state entry actions here\n(play a sound, start a timer) and they run once per transition, never per frame.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          290
        ],
        "size": [
          2360,
          810
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "cs",
          "cs_get_state",
          "cs_prev",
          "cs_state",
          "cs_reset",
          "cs_switch",
          "cs_log0",
          "cs_log1",
          "cs_log2",
          "cs_log3",
          "cs_log4"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. TICK - run the active state. ticks_in_state is incremented first, then Switch on Int\n(Case0..Case3, Default) selects behaviour. Each state here only waits `ticks_per_state` frames and\nthen asks for the next state (Idle > Patrol > Chase > Attack > Idle). The Default pin is the Dead\nstate and does nothing: it is terminal. Replace a branch with real logic (move toward the\nplayer in Chase, deal damage in Attack) and keep the transition test next to it.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          1310
        ],
        "size": [
          3040,
          960
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.35,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "tk",
          "tk_g_t",
          "tk_add",
          "tk_set_t",
          "tk_g_s",
          "tk_switch",
          "tk_idle_len",
          "tk_idle_done",
          "tk_idle_if",
          "tk_idle_go",
          "tk_patrol_len",
          "tk_patrol_done",
          "tk_patrol_if",
          "tk_patrol_go",
          "tk_chase_len",
          "tk_chase_done",
          "tk_chase_if",
          "tk_chase_go",
          "tk_attack_len",
          "tk_attack_done",
          "tk_attack_if",
          "tk_attack_go"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-5",
        "text": "4. GLOBAL TRANSITION - damage can arrive in ANY state, so it is its own entry point rather than a\nbranch inside every state. `On Damage` fires on this object (self scope). Take 25 health per\nhit; at zero or below force the Dead state. Putting such \"from any state\" transitions in\nseparate events keeps the Switch small.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          2460
        ],
        "size": [
          2360,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.8,
          0.3,
          0.3,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "dm",
          "dm_hp",
          "dm_sub",
          "dm_set",
          "dm_dead",
          "dm_if",
          "dm_go"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "custom_event_defs": {}
